note evacnote Evacuees' camp note | WE CAME OUT OF THE TOWER ON DAY 9\n\nNine of us, the night shift. The lower floors went first, all at once, as if somebody had pulled a plug. Then the lobby lights - not the storm, the board, the Director's office turning them off one by one from a hundred miles away.\nDr Sato stayed to send the drives. She said she would follow when the bees were settled. We waited two days for her here.\nA diver came past on day 11, asking after a shuttle. Then an old man with hens in a basket, asking after the diver. We gave them both our last tin of peaches and pointed at the tower.\nThe tower leans a little more every morning. We are leaving by the old road.
note yardcrate Loading yard crate | A crate never loaded onto the lab's lift: bolts, cable.
loot yardcrate Bolt*4;Rope*2;Scrap*3
prop yardcrate loot.refill=0
prop viewzone zone.id=brinelab_view
prop viewzone zone.radius=7
prop viewzone zone.repeat=never
prop viewzone zone.message=From here the lean is plain: the lab tower tilts out of its drowned pit, each floor a hand's width further out than the one below.

