# --- Settings, notes, behaviours, quest ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Brinelab Tower
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The Pelagic Network's lab tower, leaning in a drowned pit: dry labs and a hive garden above the water, five flooded floors below. The third island of The Sunken Kingdom.
island on.arrive=message||A tower leaning out of the sea, its lower windows dark with water. A plaza beside it, and a door at the waterline.

note safetyboard Lab safety board | BRINELAB - SAFETY BOARD (amended by Dr M. Sato)\n\n1. The lower floors are SEALED. Do not open the hatch below the lobby. (Unless you are me.)\n2. Data goes on drives, three copies, one per floor, because the Network trusts nothing it cannot drop in the sea.\n3. Boars are NOT lab animals. Whoever let them into the greenhouse owes me eleven tomatoes.\n4. Lights off after dark, by order of the Director. Yes, Director. I will do my sums by moonlight like a poet.\n\nUnder it, in chalk: "Sato - the shuttle stopped here at six for tea. Twelve aboard. Did they say where next? - I.M."\nAnd under that, Sato's reply: "The Caisson Yard road. I gave them biscuits. Go up to the roof, Ines, I'll tell you there."
note reception Reception drawer | The reception drawer: machete plans and a visitor's badge.
note lab2cabinet Lab 2 cabinet | A lab cabinet: fuel tank plans, labelled "for the shuttle".
note satonote Dr Sato's roof recording | RECORDER, LEFT ON THE BEEHIVE - DR M. SATO\n\nInes. You climbed all those stairs with a hen-keeper's oxygen tank on your back, so here is the truth, as much as I have.\nThe shuttle went on down the Caisson Yard road. The radio heard it hit the reef off the yard and then twelve small voices counting each other on the rocks. Twelve. All of them. They walked.\nNow the other thing. Someone sank my lower floors. Not the storm - the pumps went to REMOTE, and the command came down the wire with a name on it. I copied it onto drive 3 before the water took the room.\nGo down, read it, and then go to Wren at Biome Seven. She has the only boat left on the shelf and she will feed you melon whether you want it or not.\nThe bees say hello.
note drive1 Data drive 1 | DRIVE 1 / 3 - BIOME PROGRAMME (voice log, Dr M. Sato)\n\nSeven sealed domes on the shelf, each its own little world. Six have gone dark, one after another, the way windows go dark in a street at night.\nBiome Seven is the last one still breathing. Its gardener, Wren, sends me a melon report every Sunday whether I ask or not. This Sunday: "Melons excellent. Morale fair. Do not come down, the light is wrong out here."\nI asked her what she meant by wrong. She said: "It moves when the current doesn't."\nCopies 2 and 3 of this drive are below, where the water is. I am not going down there today. I am going to the roof to see the bees, who at least have the decency to buzz.
note drive2 Data drive 2 | DRIVE 2 / 3 - BIOME SEVEN\n\nCoordinates follow. Dome at eighteen metres, airlock on the dome's landward side. The gardener is Wren Ashby. She stays down there. She says the melons do better than we do, which is true, and that she does better than we do, which is also true.\nShelf note: Biome Seven's beacon is on this lab's transmitter. If the tower loses power the dome goes quiet with it.\n(In the margin, Sato's pencil: "copy 3 is one floor further down. Mind your head on the pipes. I didn't.")
note drive3 Data drive 3 | DRIVE 3 / 3 - TRANSMIT\n\nLast order still on the drive: "send Biome Seven's beacon to anyone who reads this". Sending.\n\nCopied by hand underneath, by Dr Sato:\n"02:14 - PUMP CONTROL: LOCAL to REMOTE.\n02:14 - VALVE COMMAND: SPIRE. Flood levels 1 to 4.\n02:15 - Message attached, voice of the Director: 'This is the Sealkeeper. Brinelab, I am sorry. It is quieter this way.'"\n\nQuieter for whom, Halvard?\nI am sending Wren's beacon anyway. If you are reading this, the Receiver will hear Biome Seven now. Go to the dome on the shelf. Wren has a boat, and she will want to know about the light.
note pipestore Pipe store | Shelves of pipe and a sealed tube of plans: fuel pipes.
note labstores Lab stores | The lab's deep store: explosive goo in sealed jars, scrap.
note boilerlocker Boiler room locker | The boiler man's locker: biofuel extractor plans and gloves.
loot reception Blueprint_Machete*1;Machete*1;Rope*2
prop reception loot.refill=0
loot lab2cabinet Blueprint_Fueltank*1;Blueprint_HeadLight*1;Bolt*2
prop lab2cabinet loot.refill=0
loot pipestore Blueprint_Pipe_Fuel*1;Blueprint_Recycler*1;Scrap*3
prop pipestore loot.refill=0
loot labstores ExplosiveGoo*2;Scrap*6
prop labstores loot.refill=0
loot boilerlocker Blueprint_BiofuelExtractor*1;BioFuel*1;Leather*1
prop boilerlocker loot.refill=0

prop atriumvines obj.name=atriumvines
prop atriumvines on.use=hide|atriumvines\nmessage||The machete bites through the vines. The hatch to the stairwell is free.
prop drive2 on.read=show|drive3\nmessage||Drive 2 names a third copy, one floor further down.
prop drive3 obj.name=drive3
prop drive3 beh.hidden=1
prop drive3 on.read=signal||drives\nmessage||The drive's last order runs: a beacon wakes somewhere on the shelf.
prop lobbyzone zone.id=lobby
prop lobbyzone zone.radius=3.5
prop lobbyzone zone.message=The lobby. Water laps at the door; a hatch in the corner is grown shut with vines.
prop stairzone zone.id=stairwell
prop stairzone zone.radius=2.5
prop stairzone zone.message=Up through the hatch - and something snorts among the planters.
prop boars creature.count=3
prop boars creature.respawn=0
prop boars creature.zone=stairwell
prop rats creature.count=3
prop rats creature.respawn=0

note bl_cavechest Cold store chest | A cold store chest: sample jars, cracked, and the lab's spare glass.
loot bl_cavechest Glass*3;Rope*2;Bolt*2;Plastic*3
prop bl_cavechest loot.refill=0
note bl_ruinnote Sample keeper's list | SAMPLE KEEPER'S LIST\n\n1. Kelp, shelf edge. Smells of feet.\n2. Water, 18 m, for the dome. Wren asks for it every month like it is wine.\n3. Something from the trench. Do not open. Do not shake. Do not, Pieter, put it near the window again.\nThe thing from the trench glows when the lights go out. Faintly. Teal. I moved it here, then to the cave, then I moved myself a long way from both.\nThe tower leans a little more each spring. The drives stay in the tower. They are the lab's memory, and Sato says a lab without a memory is just a building full of mugs.
note bl_wrecknote Crane driver's note | CRANE DRIVER'S NOTE\n\nWe were lifting the lab's cage crates when the tower moved. The crane stopped, the van stopped, I ran, and I am not ashamed of it - I have legs for a reason.\nThe bolt cutters for the cages are in the van's crate. The dome's gardener keeps animals in a cage down there and she will need them one day.\nFunny thing. The tower did not move by itself. I heard the pumps cough and stop, all of them, at the same second, like an orchestra at the end of a song. Pumps don't do that. People do that.
note bl_wreckcrate Lab van crate | The lab van's crate: the cage crew's bolt cutters and their spares.
loot bl_wreckcrate story:raft-Vasagatan_BoltCutter*1;Bolt*3;MetalIngot*1
prop bl_wreckcrate loot.refill=0

# --- DEEP 1-HOUR (10-24): story items, notes and checks
story bl_key|Pump house key|Hinge|The lab pump house's key, from the chest at the bottom of the cold well.
story sk_crest|Kingdom crest shard|Bolt|A shard of the Sunken Kingdom's crest, from a drowned building. The Hollow's crown vault wants nine.
note bldeep Pump house chest | The pump keeper's chest: his wages and a crest shard.
loot bldeep story:sk_crest*1;MetalIngot*2;Bolt*3;OxygenBottle*1;TradeToken*2
prop bldeep loot.refill=0
note bllocker Weather mast locker | The gauge reader's field kit, left on Brine Hill.
loot bllocker MetalIngot*3;CopperIngot*2;Rope*3;Cooked_Potato*2
prop bllocker loot.refill=0
note blsumnote Weather log | BRINE HILL WEATHER LOG - GAUGE READER\n\nWind off the sea, sea rising. Third reading this week the gauge went under, and I went under with it to read it, because the Network does not accept "about".\nFrom up here the whole shelf is lit by one thing: the Spirecrest beacon, far off over the water, blinking like a lighthouse that has forgotten what it is for.\nUnder the sea, past the tower, there is another light that does not blink. It moves. I have stopped writing that one down, because the Director's office keeps sending the page back.
note blbldnote Pump keeper's slate | PUMP KEEPER\n\nThe well pumps brine to the tower's drives. Twenty years, never missed a day, never dropped a bolt.\nThen the board in this house went REMOTE on its own and every valve opened together, and the well became the sea.\nI ran up the stairs, and the stairs held, which is more than I can say for the Network.\nThere is air on the first floor. The chest at the bottom has my wages in it, and the crest shard the old king's people left on the lintel. Take them. I am not coming back for either.
note blledge Gauge reader's cache | A cache on a ledge of Brine Hill, where the gauge reader sheltered.
loot blledge Rope*3;Bolt*2;Feather*3
prop blledge loot.refill=0
note blcave2chest Brine sampler's chest | A brine sampler's chest at the back of the rock cave.
loot blcave2chest CopperOre*3;Rope*2;Battery*1
prop blcave2chest loot.refill=0
prop blsummit zone.id=bl_summit
prop blsummit zone.radius=2.5
prop blsummit zone.message=The top of Brine Hill. The whole island lies below.

quest title=The Lab Tower
quest intro=The shuttle stopped at this leaning tower for tea. Go in at the waterline.
step reach|lobby|1|Go into the lobby at the waterline
step read|Lab safety board|1|Read the safety board in the lobby
step blueprint|Blueprint_Machete|1|Take the machete plans (and the caretaker's old machete) from the reception drawer
step reach|stairwell|1|Cut the vines over the hatch with the machete and climb up
